JSON files normally use the.jsonextension.

Use thefetch()method to request the JSON file.

Theresponse.json()method parses the JSON text and returns a JavaScript value.

If the file contains a JSON array,response.json()returns a JavaScript array.

Thefetch()method does not throw an error forHTTP errorssuch as 404.

Check theokandstatusproperties before reading the JSON file.

Usetry...catchto handle loading errors.

Independent downloads can run in parallel.

The fetch() method can alsosend JSONto a web server.

Use thePOSTmethod to send new data.

Convert the JavaScript object to JSON text withJSON.stringify().

Thesecond argumentof fetch() contains the request options.

TheContent-Typeheader tells the server what type of data is being sent.

The request body must contain text, not a JavaScript object.

UseJSON.stringify()to convert the object into JSON text.

A server can return JSON after receiving the request.

Useresponse.json()to read the returned JSON.

The fetch() method does not reject its Promise forHTTP errorssuch as 404 or 500.

Check theresponse.okproperty before reading the response.

Usetry...catchto handle request and response errors.

This example sends form data to a server as JSON.

